course: dictionary
lesson: 12139
title: Sharing meaning: communication
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Communication means sharing information, ideas or feelings with other people. You can do it by talking, writing, using signs or sending a message. «Maya gave her friend a smile and a thumbs up, and that was all the communication they needed.» No words were spoken, but a message still got across.
explain: Good communication at school means listening carefully, speaking clearly and taking turns. «Please wait until Ben has finished before you speak.» The teacher is helping the class communicate well by making sure everyone gets a turn to share.
explain: The word also has other meanings. A communication can be a formal message or letter, as in «The school sent a communication to all parents.» Communications can also mean the systems we use to send information, such as phones, radio and the internet. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Communication means sharing information, ideas or feelings.
fact: You can communicate by talking, writing, signs, pictures or other ways.
fact: «Communications» can mean the systems that send information, such as phones, radio and the internet.
fact: Animals communicate too: bees dance to show other bees where to find flowers, and whales sing songs.
fact: In an emergency, knowing how to communicate, such as calling 999 or 911, can save lives.
exercise: «The school sent a communication to all parents about the trip.» In this sentence, communication means what? | A game played with a ball | *A formal message or letter | A loud noise in the playground | A type of bird
exercise: Which of these is an example of communication without speaking? | *Waving hello to a friend across the playground | Eating lunch alone | Sitting still and thinking to yourself | Shutting the door quietly
exercise: Which word best completes this sentence? Good ___ means listening carefully and taking turns. | Calculation | Celebration | *Communication | Decoration
test: «The message came through the radio and the phone line.» What kind of communication is a radio? | A school subject | A tasty snack | A kind of animal call | *A system for sending information
test: Bees dance to show other bees where to find flowers. What is this an example of? | A type of weather | A school timetable | *Animal communication | A cooking recipe
exam: Which phrase describes ways of sending information from one place to another? | Hot chocolate | Long division | Blue sky | *Lines of communication
